@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/claims/{claimId}/split — split an amount (body {amount, user}), more than
+# 0.00 and less than the claim's amount, off an OPEN claim. The claim keeps the rest of its amount and is
+# unbound from any figure a statement bound it to; a new OPEN claim with the amount split off, the same
+# date and note, the next number, opened by the user, split-from the claim's number and due by its date
+# plus the terms in force on that date (fixed now) is listed as its person's newest claim. Refused (400)
+# when the amount does not parse or is out of range, the claim is not OPEN (PENDING, deferred on the
+# sheet's today, settled, ...) or not on the sheet, its date falls in a closed period, or the sheet's
+# permission matrix does not allow the user's role to open a claim; nothing is stored then. A stored
+# split is recorded in the audit file as CLAIM_SPLIT, then CLAIM_OPENED for the new claim.
+validate:
+  class: net.officefloor.hq.app.claim.ValidateSplit
+  next: load
+load:
